00:23:59,820 --> 00:24:02,080
So without knowing how big a fit is,

527
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:04,420
how should a bootloader know what to hash?

528
00:24:04,420 --> 00:24:05,820
And then it can have some flags

529
00:24:05,820 --> 00:24:08,060
for backwards and forward compatibility.

530
00:24:08,060 --> 00:24:10,180
And if you have a fit header,

